#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_or

#% text
# `bit_or(n1, n2, ...)` gives the bitwise or of the integers.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Negative integers are taken in two's complement. `bit_or()` is 0. `bit_or` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_or(12, 10)
#% output
#= 14

#% cell
bit_or(1, 2, 4, 8)
#% output
#= 15

#% cell
bit_or(-8, 3)
#% output
#= -5

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `and` plus `or` is the sum:

#% cell
[bit_and(37, 22) + bit_or(37, 22), 37 + 22]
#% output
#= [59, 59]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bit_and`, `bit_xor`, `bit_not`
